hypotheses.evidence:
Lab in-sample descriptive (results/r2/leadlag/descriptive/relative_strength_us_indices.csv, 2013-21), ranking at 10:00 on the move since 09:30 and holding the strongest minus the weakest of the three to the close:
- all days: +2.69 bp (t 2.92, n 1,982, sd 41 bp), 7 of 8 years positive (2015 -1.94; 2021 +5.37, the best year, so no erosion in sample);
- top 50 % of dispersion: +4.71 bp (t 3.03);
- top 25 %: +8.06 bp (t 3.19);
- weaker when ranked later: 10:30 top-25 % +4.35 (t 1.93), 11:00 +2.39 (t 1.16), 15:30 -0.45 (t -1.80).
This cell is the best of 48 (8 ranking times x 2 references x 3 dispersion cuts), so it should shrink out of sample.
Engine per-leg trials (results/r2/leadlag/trials.jsonl, rule 'relstr'): leg PF 0.96-1.21, t <= 1.79; trading each leg on its own carries that leg's market noise and stops it separately.
Published: only the market-level effect (Gao, Han, Li & Zhou 2018 JFE 'Market intraday momentum'; Baltussen, Da, Lammers & Martens 2021 JFE 'Hedging demand and market intraday momentum'). I know of no published test of the cross-index relative version.

hypotheses.gross_edge_needed_bp:
Cost per trade (to be replaced by FP's own cross quotes read in MT5): the synthetic two-leg spread from the lab's 2019-21 medians (results/r2/autopsy/breadth/inventory_instruments.csv), plus 0.2 bp slippage and about 0.3-0.8 bp of swap a night over about 3 nights:
- AUDNZD 1.37 + 1.92 = 3.3 bp;
- EURGBP 0.64 + 0.75 = 1.4 bp;
- AUDCAD 1.37 + 0.90 = 2.3 bp;
- NZDCAD 1.92 + 0.90 = 2.8 bp.
All-in about 3-5 bp; 2x cost = 6-10 bp.
t >= 2.5 on basket daily sums (about 350 trades, trade sd about 60-80 bp) needs net >= about 9 bp, i.e. gross >= about 13 bp per trade: about 10-15 % of the 1.5-sd deviation must revert within the hold.

hypotheses.evidence:
Published: Baur & Lucey (2010, Financial Review) and Baur & McDermott (2010, Journal of Banking & Finance): gold is a short-lived safe haven; it rises on days of extreme equity losses and then gives the gain back.
Lab, round 1, at Dukascopy costs (results/crossasset/report.md):
- after DAX 5 %-tail down days gold falls 21 bp the next day; after up days it rises 7 bp (t about 1.6);
- A3b 'follow' (gold kept as a hedge 16:30->21:00 London): gross PF 0.808 (n 357);
- A3b 'give-back over 3 days': gross PF 1.262, net PF 1.080 (n 245, t 0.50).
Weak, and the family has been tried before.

